  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "hi, it seems the team plans to push forward sdk3 more aggressively now. As it stands, there are still a few issues that will particularly plague new creators and I am hoping those could be mitigated by the time udon enters its Beta.\n\nThe core issue is that even for simple buttons you need to have multiple nodes set up and make a script for it. Think a simple mirror toggle button, that is 4 nodes, now what if you want to turn other mirrors off at the same time, we are at 5/6. This somewhat compounds ofc. Compared to sdk2 which just lets you add a trigger and put the Game Objects in there, this unnecessary complicates the creation process.\n\nOver the past year a few early adopters of sdk3 (in particular: Vowgan, Dooly and Cyan) were looking to bring dead simple and easy to use scripts to sdk3, which would essentially be used like the triggers now. Since then CyanLaser has stepped in to create CyanTriggers, which retains simplicity of sdk2 and opens users up to the freedom of sdk3 development (now or later). What you have got here is a best case scenario to utilize. And on top of his systems you also have a conversion system at disposal, that might even work on existing uploads. All in all a true on-ramp.\n\nEven with such a great tool, many creators will not know of its existence. You would expect it is simple to make something for vrchat if you download the sdk (like it is with sdk2 rn). Additionally, having to rely on another 3. party to update such a useful tool seems somewhat reckless.\nSo what I am proposing is to integrate CyanTriggers to the SDK3 by default and have it as an option for anyone looking to bring their World to life.\nAev has mentioned that you are looking into a potential integration back in March and is aware of Cyan's progress on that plugin.\nIdeally you are actually going to buy his codebase or pay Cyan for his efforts to make it work and easy for you to maintain. You should have the funds for this, and of course you also have the option to recreate such functionality on your end from scratch.\n\nPlease give this consideration, as this is the key element for a smooth transition to this better SDK.\nIf you got more questions or something is unclear, feel free to hit me up anytime.",
